* generic MPC model of a two-winding common-mode choke, generated by cmc_mpc.ltspice from circuit.mpc_netlist
* Inductor dots sit at the first node of each inductor.
* Parameters: LC CC RC (CM block), LD CD RD (DM block), CW and Lw Cwt Rw (interwinding path YW),
* Rcr Ccr (R-C branch) and Rrl Lrl (R-L branch) across each CM winding, Cg (port to ground), RDC (winding resistance).
* Unused parts are switched off by value: Lw=1e-12 shorts the LCR tank, Ccr=1e-18 and Rrl=1e12 remove the branches,
* Cg=1e-18 and RDC=1e-6 remove ground capacitance and winding resistance. The defaults are a neutral starting point.
.subckt MPC port1 port2 port3 port4 params:
+ LC=0.01 CC=3e-12 RC=30000 LD=7e-06 CD=3e-12 RD=16000 CW=3e-12 Lw=1e-12 Cwt=1e-15 Rw=1e+06 Rcr=1e+06 Ccr=1e-18 Rrl=1e+12 Lrl=0.001 Cg=1e-18 RDC=1e-06
Rs1 port1 q1 {RDC/2}
Rs2 port2 q2 {RDC/2}
Rs3 port3 q3 {RDC/2}
Rs4 port4 q4 {RDC/2}
Lc1 q1 a1 {LC/2}
Lc3 q3 a3 {LC/2}
Cc1 q1 a1 {CC}
Rc1 q1 a1 {RC}
Rcr1_0 q1 xcr1_0 {Rcr}
Ccr1_0 xcr1_0 a1 {Ccr}
Rrl1_0 q1 xrl1_0 {Rrl}
Lrl1_0 xrl1_0 a1 {Lrl}
Cc3 q3 a3 {CC}
Rc3 q3 a3 {RC}
Rcr3_0 q3 xcr3_0 {Rcr}
Ccr3_0 xcr3_0 a3 {Ccr}
Rrl3_0 q3 xrl3_0 {Rrl}
Lrl3_0 xrl3_0 a3 {Lrl}
Ld1 a1 m1 {LD/8}
Ld2 m1 q2 {LD/8}
Ld3 m3 a3 {LD/8}
Ld4 q4 m3 {LD/8}
Cd1 a1 q2 {CD}
Rd1 a1 q2 {RD}
Cd3 a3 q4 {CD}
Rd3 a3 q4 {RD}
Cw m1 w1 {CW}
Lw w1 m3 {Lw}
